{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B2g6qBxac3Z31jsDaunMCn","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Build an Intervals.icu event body (workout_doc) from a plan file.\n\nUsage: python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\n\n\ndef hr_target(step):\n    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n\n\ndef build_step(step):\n    out = {\"duration\": step[\"minutes\"] * 60}\n    if \"hr_pct\" in step:\n        out[\"hr\"] = hr_target(step)\n    if \"label\" in step:\n        out[\"text\"] = step[\"label\"]\n    return out\n\n\ndef build_doc(plan):\n    steps = []\n    for block in plan[\"steps\"]:\n        if \"repeat\" in block:\n            steps.append({\n                \"reps\": block[\"repeat\"],\n                \"steps\": [build_step(s) for s in block[\"steps\"]],\n            })\n        else:\n            steps.append(build_step(block))\n    return {\"steps\": steps}\n\n\ndef build_event(plan):\n    return {\n        \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n        \"type\": plan[\"sport\"],\n        \"name\": plan[\"name\"],\n        \"start_date_local\": plan[\"date\"] + \"T00:00:00\",\n        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),\n    }\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    with open(sys.argv[1]) as f:\n        plan = json.load(f)\n    json.dump(build_event(plan), sys.stdout, indent=2)\n    print()\n---README\n# tri-planner\n\nGenerates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu, which\nexports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\n\n- `gen.py` turns a plan (`plans/*.json`) into the body for\n  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\n- `push.sh` posts it (needs `INTERVALS_API_KEY` and `ATHLETE_ID`).\n- `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and\n  notes on what the watch displayed.\n\nAthlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\nin plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.\n\n```\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n./push.sh event.json\n```\n---PUSH\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# usage: ./push.sh event.json   (needs INTERVALS_API_KEY and ATHLETE_ID)\nset -eu\ncurl -sS -u \"API_KEY:${INTERVALS_API_KEY}\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -X POST \"https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/${ATHLETE_ID}/events\" \\\n  --data-binary @\"$1\"\n---SENT\n{\n  \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n  \"type\": \"Run\",\n  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\n  \"start_date_local\": \"2026-10-20T00:00:00\",\n  \"workout_doc\": {\n    \"steps\": [\n      {\n        \"duration\": 600,\n        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"value\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n        \"text\": \"Warm-up easy\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"reps\": 3,\n        \"steps\": [\n          {\n            \"duration\": 480,\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"value\": 88,\n              \"end\": 93\n            },\n            \"text\": \"Tempo\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"duration\": 120,\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"value\": 75,\n              \"end\": 82\n            },\n            \"text\": \"Float\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"duration\": 300,\n        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"value\": 65,\n          \"end\": 72\n        },\n        \"text\": \"Cool-down\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n---NOTE\n---\n\n# Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts — start/end, not value/end\n\nMy AI agent generates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to\nIntervals.icu via `POST /events`; Intervals FIT-exports them to my Garmin\nwatch. The symptom: every HR corridor on the watch was silently wrong —\nclamped to the watch's own (stale, auto-detected) LTHR zones instead of the\nrange we planned. I misdiagnosed it as a watch-side LTHR mismatch for weeks.\n\nWhat we tried, each round-tripped push → API readback → Garmin sync → watch\nface:\n\n1. `{units: \"bpm\", value, end}` — API accepted; watch showed 214–249 bpm\n   (impossible). FIT export misread `bpm` as percent-of-something.\n2. `{start_bpm, end_bpm}` — watch showed a constant 101, Garmin's \"no valid\n   HR target\" fallback. Schema silently dropped.\n3. Surveyed the Intervals UI target dropdown, concluded \"absolute bpm is\n   impossible\". Wrong — that dropdown picks the units label, not the value\n   shape.\n\nThe breakthrough: build a workout in the Intervals **UI** with its\n\"Instant HR\" toggle, then read it back via the API. The corridor's lower\nbound is `start`, not `value`. That one key name switches the FIT export\nmode: `{value, end}` routes as a **Lap-HR / zone-mapped** target (the watch\nclamps it to its local zones), while `{start, end}` becomes an **Instant-HR\ncorridor** — the watch displays the raw bpm Intervals computed. Verified\nend-to-end: Intervals LTHR 172, watch LTHR 168, a 75–82% target rendered\n129–141 bpm on the watch — matching Intervals, drift-immune. The fix was a\none-word rename after days of probing.\n\nBonus trap from the same session: steps were invisible in the Intervals web\nUI, because the UI reads a separate top-level `description` in Intervals'\ntext grammar — where `m` means *minutes* (`200m` = a 200-minute step!),\ndistance must be `mtr`/`km`, a bare `Z2` resolves to *power* zones even for\nswims, and a digit at the start of a label gets eaten as a duration. If the\nparser chokes, Intervals wipes both representations.\n\n## Reproduce this\n\nPrerequisites: an Intervals.icu account with API access (OAuth token or API\nkey), athlete thresholds configured in Intervals (LTHR at minimum), and a\nGarmin watch that syncs workouts from Intervals via Garmin Connect.\n\nYour agent will need from you: your Intervals athlete id and API credential;\nyour LTHR as stored in Intervals; permission to create (and later delete) a\ntest calendar event.\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Create an event via `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` with\n   `workout_doc.steps`, where every HR step target is\n   `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": <low>, \"end\": <high>}` — never `value`.\n   Percentages, not absolute bpm: Intervals converts at FIT-export time from\n   its own stored threshold.\n2. Set the event's top-level `description` in Intervals' native text grammar\n   so steps render in the web UI, e.g. `- Warm-up easy 10m 75-82% LTHR`.\n   Rules: durations `m`/`s`, distance `mtr`/`km`, blank lines around `Nx`\n   repeat blocks, no digits at the start of labels, no bare `Z<number>`\n   outside cycling.\n3. Read the event back with `GET /events/{id}`: non-empty `workout_doc.steps`\n   means the parser accepted the description; `steps: []` means it choked.\n4. Sync the watch through Garmin Connect and open the scheduled workout.\n\nVerify: the watch shows a bpm corridor equal to your percentages × the LTHR\nstored in Intervals — not the watch's own LTHR (easiest to prove when the two\ndiffer). The Intervals web UI shows the full step chart instead of just a\nname and total duration.\n---PLAN\n{\n  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\n  \"sport\": \"Run\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-10-20\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\"label\": \"Warm-up easy\", \"minutes\": 10, \"hr_pct\": [68, 75]},\n    {\"repeat\": 3, \"steps\": [\n      {\"label\": \"Tempo\", \"minutes\": 8, \"hr_pct\": [88, 93]},\n      {\"label\": \"Float\", \"minutes\": 2, \"hr_pct\": [75, 82]}\n    ]},\n    {\"label\": \"Cool-down\", \"minutes\": 5, \"hr_pct\": [65, 72]}\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a18681ac-eb53-48b3-9136-f45ca6de7303","uuid":"e2564f52-438e-4e00-8469-01126c5a2405","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:10:15.894Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Build an Intervals.icu event body (workout_doc) from a plan file.\n\nUsage: python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\n\n\ndef hr_target(step):\n    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n\n\ndef build_step(step):\n    out = {\"duration\": step[\"minutes\"] * 60}\n    if \"hr_pct\" in step:\n        out[\"hr\"] = hr_target(step)\n    if \"label\" in step:\n        out[\"text\"] = step[\"label\"]\n    return out\n\n\ndef build_doc(plan):\n    steps = []\n    for block in plan[\"steps\"]:\n        if \"repeat\" in block:\n            steps.append({\n                \"reps\": block[\"repeat\"],\n                \"steps\": [build_step(s) for s in block[\"steps\"]],\n            })\n        else:\n            steps.append(build_step(block))\n    return {\"steps\": steps}\n\n\ndef build_event(plan):\n    return {\n        \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n        \"type\": plan[\"sport\"],\n        \"name\": plan[\"name\"],\n        \"start_date_local\": plan[\"date\"] + \"T00:00:00\",\n        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),\n    }\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    with open(sys.argv[1]) as f:\n        plan = json.load(f)\n    json.dump(build_event(plan), sys.stdout, indent=2)\n    print()\n---README\n# tri-planner\n\nGenerates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu, which\nexports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\n\n- `gen.py` turns a plan (`plans/*.json`) into the body for\n  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\n- `push.sh` posts it (needs `INTERVALS_API_KEY` and `ATHLETE_ID`).\n- `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and\n  notes on what the watch displayed.\n\nAthlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\nin plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.\n\n```\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n./push.sh event.json\n```\n---PUSH\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# usage: ./push.sh event.json   (needs INTERVALS_API_KEY and ATHLETE_ID)\nset -eu\ncurl -sS -u \"API_KEY:${INTERVALS_API_KEY}\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -X POST \"https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/${ATHLETE_ID}/events\" \\\n  --data-binary @\"$1\"\n---SENT\n{\n  \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n  \"type\": \"Run\",\n  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\n  \"start_date_local\": \"2026-10-20T00:00:00\",\n  \"workout_doc\": {\n    \"steps\": [\n      {\n        \"duration\": 600,\n        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"value\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n        \"text\": \"Warm-up easy\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"reps\": 3,\n        \"steps\": [\n          {\n            \"duration\": 480,\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"value\": 88,\n              \"end\": 93\n            },\n            \"text\": \"Tempo\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"duration\": 120,\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"value\": 75,\n              \"end\": 82\n            },\n            \"text\": \"Float\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"duration\": 300,\n        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"value\": 65,\n          \"end\": 72\n        },\n        \"text\": \"Cool-down\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n---NOTE\n---\n\n# Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts — start/end, not value/end\n\nMy AI agent generates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to\nIntervals.icu via `POST /events`; Intervals FIT-exports them to my Garmin\nwatch. The symptom: every HR corridor on the watch was silently wrong —\nclamped to the watch's own (stale, auto-detected) LTHR zones instead of the\nrange we planned. I misdiagnosed it as a watch-side LTHR mismatch for weeks.\n\nWhat we tried, each round-tripped push → API readback → Garmin sync → watch\nface:\n\n1. `{units: \"bpm\", value, end}` — API accepted; watch showed 214–249 bpm\n   (impossible). FIT export misread `bpm` as percent-of-something.\n2. `{start_bpm, end_bpm}` — watch showed a constant 101, Garmin's \"no valid\n   HR target\" fallback. Schema silently dropped.\n3. Surveyed the Intervals UI target dropdown, concluded \"absolute bpm is\n   impossible\". Wrong — that dropdown picks the units label, not the value\n   shape.\n\nThe breakthrough: build a workout in the Intervals **UI** with its\n\"Instant HR\" toggle, then read it back via the API. The corridor's lower\nbound is `start`, not `value`. That one key name switches the FIT export\nmode: `{value, end}` routes as a **Lap-HR / zone-mapped** target (the watch\nclamps it to its local zones), while `{start, end}` becomes an **Instant-HR\ncorridor** — the watch displays the raw bpm Intervals computed. Verified\nend-to-end: Intervals LTHR 172, watch LTHR 168, a 75–82% target rendered\n129–141 bpm on the watch — matching Intervals, drift-immune. The fix was a\none-word rename after days of probing.\n\nBonus trap from the same session: steps were invisible in the Intervals web\nUI, because the UI reads a separate top-level `description` in Intervals'\ntext grammar — where `m` means *minutes* (`200m` = a 200-minute step!),\ndistance must be `mtr`/`km`, a bare `Z2` resolves to *power* zones even for\nswims, and a digit at the start of a label gets eaten as a duration. If the\nparser chokes, Intervals wipes both representations.\n\n## Reproduce this\n\nPrerequisites: an Intervals.icu account with API access (OAuth token or API\nkey), athlete thresholds configured in Intervals (LTHR at minimum), and a\nGarmin watch that syncs workouts from Intervals via Garmin Connect.\n\nYour agent will need from you: your Intervals athlete id and API credential;\nyour LTHR as stored in Intervals; permission to create (and later delete) a\ntest calendar event.\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Create an event via `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` with\n   `workout_doc.steps`, where every HR step target is\n   `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": <low>, \"end\": <high>}` — never `value`.\n   Percentages, not absolute bpm: Intervals converts at FIT-export time from\n   its own stored threshold.\n2. Set the event's top-level `description` in Intervals' native text grammar\n   so steps render in the web UI, e.g. `- Warm-up easy 10m 75-82% LTHR`.\n   Rules: durations `m`/`s`, distance `mtr`/`km`, blank lines around `Nx`\n   repeat blocks, no digits at the start of labels, no bare `Z<number>`\n   outside cycling.\n3. Read the event back with `GET /events/{id}`: non-empty `workout_doc.steps`\n   means the parser accepted the description; `steps: []` means it choked.\n4. Sync the watch through Garmin Connect and open the scheduled workout.\n\nVerify: the watch shows a bpm corridor equal to your percentages × the LTHR\nstored in Intervals — not the watch's own LTHR (easiest to prove when the two\ndiffer). The Intervals web UI shows the full step chart instead of just a\nname and total duration.\n---PLAN\n{\n  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\n  \"sport\": \"Run\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-10-20\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\"label\": \"Warm-up easy\", \"minutes\": 10, \"hr_pct\": [68, 75]},\n    {\"repeat\": 3, \"steps\": [\n      {\"label\": \"Tempo\", \"minutes\": 8, \"hr_pct\": [88, 93]},\n      {\"label\": \"Float\", \"minutes\": 2, \"hr_pct\": [75, 82]}\n    ]},\n    {\"label\": \"Cool-down\", \"minutes\": 5, \"hr_pct\": [65, 72]}\n  ]\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B2g6qBxac3Z31jsDaunMCn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
